     1,
     "Hello, <br><br><div>I believe I have found an error in the R-INLA faq. In answer 22 (<a href=\"https://www.r-inla.org/faq#h.z4ecbkezo5tu\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.r-inla.org/faq%23h.z4ecbkezo5tu&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792434170870000&amp;usg=AOvVaw16MZdm_Q4PqqdFHWSn17yd\">https://www.r-inla.org/faq#h.z4ecbkezo5tu</a>) there is a link to a techincal report (<a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fsites.google.com%2Fa%2Fr-inla.org%2Fwww%2Ffaq%2Fwaic_understand3.pdf%3Fattredirects%3D0&amp;sa=D&amp;sntz=1&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JH_cV898Iez_DoAx-DQkA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.google.com/url?q%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Fsites.google.com%252Fa%252Fr-inla.org%252Fwww%252Ffaq%252Fwaic_understand3.pdf%253Fattredirects%253D0%26sa%3DD%26sntz%3D1%26usg%3DAOvVaw2JH_cV898Iez_DoAx-DQkA&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792434170870000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0lOYjZiMsh4QahoJp2s2CG\">in this tech-report</a>) that goes to a resource that does not exist. </div><div><br></div><div>After some digging I found a document with the same name as given in the link URL in <a href=\"https://github.com/hrue/r-inla/blob/devel/internal-doc/waic/waic_understand3.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hrue/r-inla/blob/devel/internal-doc/waic/waic_understand3.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792434170870000&amp;usg=AOvVaw25x4dR-3q_lBFVOj6brBNW\">the Github repository</a>.  This document seems to be the same as Gelman et al. 2014(<a href=\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11222-013-9416-2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11222-013-9416-2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792434170870000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0wnMy7YtIy3YLqSbybU8tR\">DOI: 10.1007/s11222-013-9416-2</a>). <br><br>Could this be changed in the faq to either cite the paper or in some other way give reference to the article to make it findable? <br><br>Thanks in advance, </div><div>Kristian</div>"
    ]
